fields.intent:
**Bring storytree's marketing website over from 0.2 so that what a first user reads matches what 0.3 is.** Opened 2026-09-30 by the owner, who wants first users to become advocates. The website is the marketing surface; the site that is live today describes 0.2. Settled in ADR-0798 (decision_67b283aa164b):
- its own story and package (`packages/website`), rebuilt small rather than ported;
- a live 3D forest drawn by the app's own engine (`@storytree/forest-world`) from a snapshot of 0.3's own library;
- published to here.now (slug `crisp-globe-bf6v`) by 0.3's CI on every merge that changes it;
- LinkedIn as the contact path;
- claims that match 0.3: PolyForm Shield, and health as the agent reported it. The install one-liner was one of them until 2026-10-02, when the owner replaced the site's install ask with a waitlist on its own arc (arc_54b5cdc7a12c, ADR-0861); the repository front page keeps the command.

This arc does NOT gate first users (ADR-0798 D7): arc_2b919de0d372's invitations point to the repository front page. The address is settled (question_188f713374ec): keep the here.now address for now, with no custom domain.

fields.endState:
Closed when the site is live on here.now from 0.3's repository:
- it is built from `packages/website`, and CI republishes it on each merge that changes it;
- its home page gives the pitch, the PolyForm Shield license and the LinkedIn contact, and makes no claim 0.3 does not keep; it states no install command, because the site's ask is the waitlist, built on its own arc (arc_54b5cdc7a12c, ADR-0861), while the repository front page keeps the command;
- its forest is the desktop app's forest-world engine drawing a snapshot of 0.3's own library, with a still where WebGL is missing, and reads well on a phone;
- the settled here.now address is kept, with no custom domain;
- after the forest and publishing are live and the owner confirms, the separate archive increment archives `storytree-ai/storytree-web`.

fields.body:
Build the site's package scaffold and home page in `packages/website`, following the plan from increment_2b67ca01952c. The forest is its own increment, increment_fd8293776dc9. Port the behaviour of 0.2's site (`C:\code\storytree\web` on the laptop, frozen; its git history is in `storytree-ai/storytree-web`), not its code. The leave-outs are listed in ADR-0798 D2.

Keep:
- the headline "Software you can watch grow.";
- the honesty lines (one person, written by AI agents);
- the 404 line.

The claims must match 0.3 (ADR-0798 D3):
- the same install one-liner as the README, from one source;
- the PolyForm Shield license;
- LinkedIn as the contact (https://www.linkedin.com/in/mick-hua-353353a/);
- health as the agent reported it.

Leave a clearly marked slot where the forest mounts. Check the page at phone width. It is a visual unit, so its look lands with its pictures (ADR-0794).

OWNER'S ANSWER 2026-10-02 (question_40e1e880b1bf): "Go with A for now, think this really should just be more of a exposure surface, your right that the agents.md should override this anyways or can pull against this. I just noticed this is something i wanted to look at from time to time without having to ask an agent. making it configurable might be on overreach at this stage"

What it means for the build (ADR-0842, D1 and D2). Today packages/agent-link/src/instructions/habits.ts says only "When only the owner can decide, raise_question on the arc", and nothing defines it. Add a few lines, inside the card's 60-line budget:
- the agent decides and records reversible engineering choices; a built look lands with its pictures;
- it asks before choosing between designs before building, before anything outward-facing, irreversible, spending money, or dropping or reshaping the work asked for;
- it checks the owner's standing delegations before asking;
- the user's own instructions file (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md) overrides this split for any kind, either way;
- never moved by any file: it never signs off its own output (a separate agent, a judge panel or CI does), never skips tests, and writes a question rather than only asking in chat.
Contract on capability 7 (Instructions): the card handed at session start names the kinds the agent decides, the kinds it asks about, that the user's instructions file overrides them, and the honesty promises. Test first against the served text's behaviour, not its wording (ADR-0623). The card's existing tests hold it to naming exactly the server's tools in backticks, so do not backtick anything new that is not a tool.

Not in scope: any setting for it (D3). The read-only view is its own increment, "See who decides what without asking an agent", and should show this same text, so land this first.
